ddressed by expanding the supported set of currency symbols within the `parseAmount` function.\n\n```typescript\nlet text = raw.replace(/[\\s\u20ac$\u00a3\u00a5\u20b9]/g, \"\");\n```\n\nHere is the conclusion for this investigation:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"issue\": 4402,\n  \"label\": \"bug\",\n  \"file\": \"src/util/money.ts\",\n  \"evidence\": \"In `parseAmount` function, only certain currency symbols (\u20ac, $, \u00a3, \u00a5) are removed from amounts. The absence of the rupee sign (\u20b9) causes the rejection of amounts containing it, leading to the error 'The amount is not a number'.\"\n}\n```\n\nI'll proceed by returning this structured finding.", "agent": "investigator-4402", "parent": "coordinator"}
